/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (It is true that people who have life-limiting conditions or illness that will lead to the end of their life receive palliative care and transition to hospice when it is needed. However, it is also true that some people with acute periods of illness recover, are cured or achieve optimized management of symptomatic disease and may no longer need palliative care services after some time.  )
/E (It is true that people who have life-limiting conditions or illness that will lead to the end of their life receive palliative care and transition to hospice when it is needed. However, it is also true that some people with acute periods of illness recover, are cured or achieve optimized management of symptomatic disease and may no longer need palliative care services after some time.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
